# Cloudflare Pages edge headers for the vault workspace.
#
# SYNTAX. Pages reads this file from the root of the SERVED directory, which is
# the build output. It therefore lives in public/, so Vite copies it verbatim to
# dist/_headers. A rule is a path pattern at column 0 followed by indented
# `Name: value` lines; a comment is a line beginning with `#` at column 0.
# Cloudflare documents comments only at column 0 and says nothing about indented
# ones, so every comment here sits at column 0 and the rule block below contains
# header lines and nothing else. Malformed lines are IGNORED RATHER THAN
# REPORTED, so a header accidentally written at column 0 becomes a path pattern
# carrying no headers and protects nothing, silently.
#
# PORTED FROM apps/site/public/_headers ON 2026-09-19, and it is narrower than
# its source in three places rather than the same file with a different name.
# Each narrowing is a class of resource the site uses and this surface does not.
# A directive that permits something nothing here loads is a standing permission
# the next person inherits without a review, which is the argument the site's own
# file makes twice -- once when the last video went and `media-src` was deleted,
# once when the chain read went and `connect-src` was narrowed.
#
# DIRECTIVE BY DIRECTIVE.
#
# default-src 'none'
#   The deny-by-default floor. Every fetch directive not named below inherits
#   it, so a directive that is absent from this file is 'none'.
#
# script-src 'self'
#   The built module scripts, served from this origin. No 'unsafe-inline' and no
#   'unsafe-eval'. Vite's modulepreload polyfill is an inline script, so
#   `build.modulePreload.polyfill` is false in vite.config.ts; without that, the
#   browser refuses the polyfill and the page's own modules may not load.
#
# style-src 'self'
#   The one built stylesheet, same-origin. Deliberately no 'unsafe-inline'.
#   THE ONE THING TO KNOW BEFORE ADDING A STYLE: React's `style={{...}}` prop
#   sets properties through the CSSOM, which this directive does not govern, so
#   ProposalPanel's vote bar (`style={{ width: `${forPct}%` }}`) works and is not
#   an exception being carved out. A literal `style="..."` in SERVED MARKUP is a
#   different thing and IS refused. This app is client-rendered, so React never
#   serialises that attribute into the HTML the edge returns -- which is exactly
#   why prerendering this surface, or server-rendering it, is a policy change and
#   not just a build change. ssr-smoke.tsx renders to a string in Node and is
#   never served, so it is not affected.
#
# img-src 'self'
#   NARROWER THAN THE SITE, which permits `data:` for a WebGL hero that builds
#   textures from data URIs. There is no canvas here and no hero. The build sets
#   no inlining exception, so every image is a file this origin served.
#
# font-src 'self'
#   The two bundled woff2 faces, shipped by the @fontsource packages into this
#   build rather than linked from a CDN. NOT `data:`: an inlined face would
#   defeat the check that every font is a file this origin served, which is how
#   the no-external-request claim is verified from the network panel. There is no
#   fonts.googleapis.com and no fonts.gstatic.com, and one request to either is a
#   rejection.
#
# connect-src 'self' https://sepolia.base.org
#   PLAN ITEM 0.7, ADDED IN THE SAME COMMIT AS `src/lib/live-vaults.ts`. This surface now reads a
#   chain through `apps/web/src/chain-reader.mjs` — see that module's header, and `live-vaults.ts`
#   for the viem glue — rather than bundling `apps/web/src/fixtures.mjs`.
#
#   THE ONE ORIGIN NAMED, NOTHING WIDER. `https://sepolia.base.org` (chain 84532) is what
#   `VITE_RPC_URL` resolves to for the ONE configuration this repository can prove end to end today
#   — `apps/vaults-ui/.env.example`, against the smoke vault in
#   `contracts/config/deployments/base-sepolia.json`. Nothing from this repository is deployed on
#   Arc mainnet (chain 5042) yet — `contracts/config/arc-mainnet.json`'s own `status` field says so
#   — so there is no Arc RPC origin to add here honestly. `test/csp.test.mjs`'s
#   `'the policy names every directive...'` test pins this exact string; widening it to a second
#   origin, a wildcard, or back to bare `'self'` must fail that test, not quietly pass it.
#
#   BEFORE THE ARC CUTOVER: replace this origin with the production RPC `VITE_RPC_URL` will be set
#   to, in the SAME COMMIT that changes the Cloudflare Pages build environment — never ahead of it.
#   A `connect-src` opened in advance of the endpoint it names is a permission nobody reviewed
#   against a chain nobody chose; a `connect-src` left behind after the endpoint changes is a page
#   that refuses its own reads with no build-time warning.
#
# worker-src IS ABSENT, AND ITS ABSENCE IS THE ENTRY.
#   The site permits a same-origin worker as headroom for moving WebGL work off
#   the main thread. There is no WebGL here and no worker. It falls back to
#   `default-src 'none'`, so `new Worker()` is refused. To put one back: add
#   `worker-src 'self'`, never `blob:`, in the same commit as the code.
#
# media-src IS ABSENT for the same reason it is absent from the site: this origin
#   serves no video and no audio, so a <video> or <audio> element is refused by
#   the browser, which is the correct answer for a surface that has none.
#
# base-uri 'none'
#   Every in-app link is relative and every off-app link is absolute. An injected
#   `<base href="https://evil.example/">` would repoint the relative ones without
#   a line of JavaScript; this refuses it.
#
# form-action 'none'
#   There is no form on this surface and no place to submit one. A workspace that
#   displays a member's own position is the obvious place to inject a credential
#   or seed-phrase prompt; injected HTML here has nowhere to POST to.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none'
#   Nobody may frame this workspace. The material risk is not clickjacking but
#   framing: this surface renders NAV, a share price and a member's position, and
#   a hostile page that frames it inside its own chrome has published the
#   protocol's numbers under someone else's name and without the disclaimers link
#   that the masthead and the footer both carry.
#
# object-src 'none'
#   Written explicitly even though default-src already covers it. Plugin content
#   is the one bypass that survives a strict script policy in older engines, and a
#   reader of this file should not have to derive its absence.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#   This origin serves .html, .css, .js, .woff2 and .woff -- @fontsource ships
#   both formats for IBM Plex Mono and the build emits both, which is why the
#   list is longer than the font-src entry above implies. Sniffing is the mechanism by
#   which a file served as one type is interpreted as another; nosniff makes the
#   declared Content-Type binding.
#
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
#   Every off-origin link from here goes to rwally.com or to the repository.
#   Without this, following one tells the destination which vault a member was
#   looking at. There is no analytics, so the strictest value costs nothing.
#
# X-Robots-Tag: noindex
#   NOT ON THE SITE, AND DELIBERATE HERE. index.html already carries
#   `<meta name="robots" content="noindex">`, but a meta tag is only read by a
#   crawler that parses the document; this covers the JSON, the stylesheet and
#   anything else served from this origin. The marketing site is the surface meant
#   to be found.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://sepolia.base.org; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# The build emits content-hashed filenames under /assets/, so those files are
# immutable by construction: a change produces a new name rather than new bytes at
# the same name. The HTML is not hashed and must not be cached that way.
#
# THAT IS A RULE ABOUT WHAT MAY LIVE UNDER /assets/, not just a note. Vite hashes
# what it processes and copies public/ through verbatim, path and all. A file
# placed at public/assets/ therefore serves from /assets/ with a FIXED name and
# inherits a year of immutable caching it cannot satisfy: replacing it would leave
# every cache that already holds it serving the old bytes until 2027, with no way
# to bust it short of renaming. Put a verbatim public asset at the root of public/.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# DELIBERATELY ABSENT, each a standard header that would do nothing here, and a
# header that does nothing is a claim of protection the next reader has to
# disprove:
#
#   X-Frame-Options    -- superseded by frame-ancestors in every browser that
#                         ships CSP Level 2.
#   Permissions-Policy -- gates browser APIs. This surface wants none.
#   X-XSS-Protection   -- removed from every current browser; its legacy scanner
#                         introduced vulnerabilities of its own.
#
# STRICT-TRANSPORT-SECURITY REMAINS THE OWNER'S DECISION, NOT THIS FILE'S, for the
# same reason as on the site: HSTS is close to irreversible, and the zone may
# already set it under Cloudflare SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates, where two sources
# would disagree.
#
#   INDENT IT UNDER A PATH PATTERN WHEN ENABLING. The line below sits at column 0,
#   and an uncommented line at column 0 is a PATH PATTERN, not a header.
#
#       Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
